#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157062 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60062061-501a-5ab1-87fc-c6fc39ea3fbc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Odd Power"}] :question/id #uuid "264fc406-4800-5084-8fb9-5d312bdbd87a" :question/math-academy-id "e-7651" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2(x - 2)^3 - 5 \\gt      11.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)^{3}-5 & >11 \\\\ 2(x-2)^{3} & >16 \\\\ (x-2)^{3} & >8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(x-2)^{3}} & >\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\ x-2 & >2 \\\\ x & >4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157063 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2463ef2-c276-53cb-a1a1-8601789574d3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power Compared To a Negative Number"}] :question/id #uuid "2d467e68-1d9b-5e6b-ab4f-663716e72c08" :question/math-academy-id "e-7652" :question/problem "Solve $(5x-1)^6 + 5 \\geq -4.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x-1)^{6}+5 & \\ge -4 \\\\ (5x-1)^{6} & \\ge -9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $(5x - 1)^{6} \\geq 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(6)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157064 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2107f945-7cfa-5abd-a6c1-bf15d5039e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power"}] :question/id #uuid "bc596174-92e8-5def-ac86-34ef18cfa3c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-7653" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(5x + 2)^4}{9} - 3 \\gt 6.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5x+2)^{4}}{9}-3 & >6 \\\\ \\frac{(5x+2)^{4}}{9} & >9 \\\\ (5x+2)^{4} & >81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{(5x+2)^{4}} & >\\sqrt[4]{81} \\\\ |5x+2| & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n5x + 2 \\lt -3 \\qquad \\textrm{or} \\qquad 5x + 2 \\gt 3\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2 & <-3 &  &  & 5x+2 & >3 \\\\ 5x & <-5 &  &  & 5x & >1 \\\\ x & <-1 &  &  & x & >\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\lt -1 \\quad \\textrm{or} \\quad x \\gt \\dfrac{1}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2107f945-7cfa-5abd-a6c1-bf15d5039e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a93e023-6e43-5c3b-9cf3-6eca2a191b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<1-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x>1+\\sqrt[6]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281927} {:answer/id #uuid "45855a7c-ba17-53d1-b64d-be17f5c1db8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>1+\\sqrt[6]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281928} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed63e80-29cc-506a-b1ad-ce050e7d3a6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-1-\\sqrt[6]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281929} {:answer/id #uuid "01124737-6c5e-5c9e-b7e3-8ff76ee8dc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281930} {:answer/id #uuid "cb3dc11d-6041-518c-b908-1614b3342e84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a93e023-6e43-5c3b-9cf3-6eca2a191b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<1-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x>1+\\sqrt[6]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281927} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab0bfeb7-ca05-59e9-a5c1-d4cf1565de8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b64255ff-f045-5b1b-b2e0-7a0c0df1a6c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-116221" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4(1-x)^{6}-1>7.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1-x)^{6}-1 & >7 \\\\ 4(1-x)^{6} & >8 \\\\ (1-x)^{6} & >2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the sixth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{(1-x)^{6}} & >\\sqrt[6]{2} \\\\ |1-x| & >\\sqrt[6]{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n1-x<-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,1-x>\\sqrt[6]{2}\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-x & <-\\sqrt[6]{2} &  &  & 1-x & >\\sqrt[6]{2} \\\\ -x & <-\\sqrt[6]{2}-1 &  &  & -x & >\\sqrt[6]{2}-1 \\\\ x & >1+\\sqrt[6]{2} &  &  & x & <1-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is\n\n$$\nx<1-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x>1+\\sqrt[6]{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2107f945-7cfa-5abd-a6c1-bf15d5039e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a2acc41-124a-50ed-b92f-af62f1a030d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>\\sqrt[4]{6}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281934} {:answer/id #uuid "953d479f-f7dd-5d8d-8a1e-3415811e97fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-\\sqrt[4]{6}-2\\,$ or $\\,x>\\sqrt[4]{6}-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281935} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed0a7ab-26f4-56dc-a9f3-bac1066f8633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\sqrt[4]{6}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281936} {:answer/id #uuid "2e225e8e-0eed-585f-a6a9-d5e4a8f12c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt[4]{6}-4<x<\\sqrt[4]{6}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281937} {:answer/id #uuid "7fbfc105-b7cb-552d-83d1-bf427302e37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\sqrt[4]{6}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e225e8e-0eed-585f-a6a9-d5e4a8f12c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt[4]{6}-4<x<\\sqrt[4]{6}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281937} :answer-field/id #uuid "e59d52a6-82e2-5979-aeea-009a3685986d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f798ab92-48c0-5ca8-a2db-e9b18af0cb6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-116224" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2(x+4)^{4}+6<18.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)^{4}+6 & <18 \\\\ 2(x+4)^{4} & <12 \\\\ (x+4)^{4} & <6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{(x+4)^{4}} & <\\sqrt[4]{6} \\\\ |x+4| & <\\sqrt[4]{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt[4]{6}<x+4<\\sqrt[4]{6}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[4]{6}<x+4 & <\\sqrt[4]{6} \\\\ -\\sqrt[4]{6}-4<x & <\\sqrt[4]{6}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2463ef2-c276-53cb-a1a1-8601789574d3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power Compared To a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfe895a1-284b-5961-b31f-07dbddfbc847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281941} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5fc4fb-2330-51cc-b8d5-b9dc712008be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281942} {:answer/id #uuid "fae32e94-8fa3-5478-a92e-c76d4a412773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281943} {:answer/id #uuid "7a3a0c65-a723-5f5a-919b-9dcd7da0c4f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281944} {:answer/id #uuid "f44a0b38-313f-5ab1-9533-31d35c6569a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fae32e94-8fa3-5478-a92e-c76d4a412773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281943} :answer-field/id #uuid "26d77f55-8a43-53f4-9a83-43bcb18a6f17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2eba8e28-81e4-514d-9e97-b76a4ae28edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-116229" :question/problem "Solve $(4x-5)^{4}+25\\le 9.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the quartic term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4x-5)^{4}+25 & \\le 9 \\\\ (4x-5)^{4} & \\le -16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(4x-5)^{4}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(4)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2463ef2-c276-53cb-a1a1-8601789574d3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power Compared To a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2b04d60-d35c-5cec-989b-cdc8c582116d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281948} {:answer/id #uuid "4fdca5ef-b0b4-50ae-8f64-32522597d945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281949} {:answer/id #uuid "98797c92-ce9c-513b-af06-1db20da15139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>\\sqrt[8]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281950} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6afedf-1bde-52b7-8e5e-d12d4f628222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281951} {:answer/id #uuid "514aba8b-ad2a-5e23-b0c5-b8fd63d3e232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2b04d60-d35c-5cec-989b-cdc8c582116d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281948} :answer-field/id #uuid "98b3b454-90e5-572f-98b6-b7f5870faf93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "395c7847-bd7c-509f-85ea-db399b921673" :question/math-academy-id "q-116241" :question/problem "Solve $2(2-5x)^{8}+7<3.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the eighth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2-5x)^{8}+7 & <3 \\\\ 2(2-5x)^{8} & <-4 \\\\ (2-5x)^{8} & <-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(2-5x)^{8}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(8)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60062061-501a-5ab1-87fc-c6fc39ea3fbc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Odd Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83475b74-f0ed-50f9-ba62-38caa4368f08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281955} {:answer/id #uuid "fcbee9b7-2d0d-53d7-84d9-e8a95542f39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcbee9b7-2d0d-53d7-84d9-e8a95542f39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281956} :answer-field/id #uuid "98b73f5c-3f13-52bd-9adf-e1e433e72260" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028c7ef9-9fde-588f-8a86-bcb67046a448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-5^{\\frac{1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "028c7ef9-9fde-588f-8a86-bcb67046a448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-5^{\\frac{1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281958} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa9f02d1-4941-574d-a7d7-931d14c9e2c5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34cd14a9-3fc5-5c65-905b-62d28d2da943" :question/math-academy-id "q-278048" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(x-6)^{3}+5\\le 0.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the cubic-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)^{3}+5 & \\le 0 \\\\ (x-6)^{3} & \\le -5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the third root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(x-6)^{3}} & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5} \\\\ x-6 & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5} \\\\ x & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5}+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60062061-501a-5ab1-87fc-c6fc39ea3fbc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Odd Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "360f013d-7ccb-5f03-801b-0de9a4162e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "360f013d-7ccb-5f03-801b-0de9a4162e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281961} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2da26d-3ea6-5b2d-8ed6-6bf8c2d99e8a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "604f1546-379b-5d72-be50-c66dd7c0b269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9^{\\frac{1}{7}}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "604f1546-379b-5d72-be50-c66dd7c0b269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9^{\\frac{1}{7}}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281963} :answer-field/id #uuid "356a5ce2-900a-5ca2-b109-ee875bbf79f8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f96d7c7-49d8-5912-9da1-cffe54ad2c27" :question/math-academy-id "q-278051" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(x+5)^{7}-1\\ge 8.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the seventh-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{7}-1 & \\ge 8 \\\\ (x+5)^{7} & \\ge 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the seventh root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[7]{(x+5)^{7}} & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{9} \\\\ x+5 & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{9} \\\\ x & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{9}-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60062061-501a-5ab1-87fc-c6fc39ea3fbc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Odd Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f56fb40-842f-548a-bf57-0d7ea0d7a1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281966} {:answer/id #uuid "1a106b92-a903-5f72-8e7e-6a3d0a29405e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a106b92-a903-5f72-8e7e-6a3d0a29405e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281967} :answer-field/id #uuid "67d20b1b-c2c0-58e4-bafc-9deebf033339" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e790864c-23ad-51d3-adf2-858c777254d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-13^{\\frac{1}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e790864c-23ad-51d3-adf2-858c777254d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-13^{\\frac{1}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281969} :answer-field/id #uuid "723f52a3-b130-5b11-b246-bb8cdfff5e1a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "457dac10-7325-5ec0-b736-38ba54dd0950" :question/math-academy-id "q-278121" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(3-x)^{7}-8\\ge 5.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the seventh-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-x)^{7}-8 & \\ge 5 \\\\ (3-x)^{7} & \\ge 13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the seventh root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[7]{(3-x)^{7}} & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13} \\\\ 3-x & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13} \\\\ -x & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13}-3 \\\\ x & \\le -\\sqrt[7]{13}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2107f945-7cfa-5abd-a6c1-bf15d5039e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98f582e2-e2be-508c-aa5d-193cf2f1175e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281972} {:answer/id #uuid "3e3e0ece-756a-569d-a148-d3a7e3091918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98f582e2-e2be-508c-aa5d-193cf2f1175e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281972} :answer-field/id #uuid "24a27655-e704-5b64-914d-d2e117a456d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281971} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3a76996-f434-5ec4-88b1-2cca71ab0dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3a76996-f434-5ec4-88b1-2cca71ab0dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281975} :answer-field/id #uuid "c14f0aff-3287-5a25-86ab-735d882d7828" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281974} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "beb4da28-d37a-5140-9b81-9a81606eb95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "beb4da28-d37a-5140-9b81-9a81606eb95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281977} :answer-field/id #uuid "dffd5c06-a1bb-52a6-8baa-ef1954725c9f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "83635496-e658-526e-b35d-174e9d817b7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-278138" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(4-x)^{2}-10\\ge 7.$\n\n$x\\le ${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the quadratic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4-x)^{2}-10 & \\ge 7 \\\\ (4-x)^{2} & \\ge 17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the square root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{17} \\\\ |4-x| & \\ge \\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n4-x\\le -\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{or}\\,4-x\\ge \\sqrt{17}\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-x & \\le -\\sqrt{17} &  &  & 4-x & \\ge \\sqrt{17} \\\\ -x & \\le -\\sqrt{17}-4 &  &  & -x & \\ge \\sqrt{17}-4 \\\\ x & \\ge 4+\\sqrt{17} &  &  & x & \\le 4-\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\le 4-\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge 4+\\sqrt{17}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2107f945-7cfa-5abd-a6c1-bf15d5039e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfc8b207-d348-59ba-adc7-6e78e0ea765c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281980} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0c52a2-5479-58ff-8b67-023e4ff23de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfc8b207-d348-59ba-adc7-6e78e0ea765c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281980} :answer-field/id #uuid "916573c7-12cb-5c86-b32c-d14ca3544486" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281979} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67bb4fe6-cbe4-5f80-9160-901fb9c97ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67bb4fe6-cbe4-5f80-9160-901fb9c97ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281983} :answer-field/id #uuid "7154e297-7210-5749-9bd2-bff4a92ee1b1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "489887c0-85df-5bf4-af0f-b34fb8907efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "489887c0-85df-5bf4-af0f-b34fb8907efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281985} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe548182-f12d-512b-b201-4ac18e828fa6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5e7cceb-3b0e-5ae1-861b-1378b9b9e348" :question/math-academy-id "q-278143" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the inequality $-4(5-x)^{6}+147>-109.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(5-x)^{6}+147 & >-109 \\\\ -4(5-x)^{6} & >-256 \\\\ (5-x)^{6} & <64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the inequality when we divided both sides by $-4.$\n\nNow, we take the sixth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{(5-x)^{6}} & <\\sqrt[6]{64} \\\\ |5-x| & <2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-2<5-x<2\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2<5-x & <2 \\\\ -7<-x & <-3 \\\\ 7>x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the lower number is on the left:\n\n$$\n3<x<7\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60062061-501a-5ab1-87fc-c6fc39ea3fbc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Odd Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9585770b-702f-5195-8b52-6be05ef3707f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156215} {:answer/id #uuid "f32f09b7-3b42-5919-bc58-503c152ac81d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156216} {:answer/id #uuid "17f384d2-3281-5d1a-9d3b-f5b053a20585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156217} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4c1f75-1a96-5205-bc4a-065994eedec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156218} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec5bf34-4c4a-55ab-a43b-abeec0ebd22b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17f384d2-3281-5d1a-9d3b-f5b053a20585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156217} :answer-field/id #uuid "397c3e38-6fa0-539c-bc37-f8a54d8b5362" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c797b467-18dd-5587-bb87-a96080eddf3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-87448" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(5-2x)^{3}-60\\ge 4.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-2x)^{3}-60 & \\ge 4 \\\\ (5-2x)^{3} & \\ge 64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(5-2x)^{3}} & \\ge \\sqrt[3]{64} \\\\ 5-2x & \\ge 4 \\\\ -2x & \\ge -1 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60062061-501a-5ab1-87fc-c6fc39ea3fbc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Odd Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e17adad3-1d87-5ef4-98ed-8ba6c2c7114c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281988} {:answer/id #uuid "222ccec3-b909-5fb5-8a6c-4aa766fa7166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281989} {:answer/id #uuid "e275f16c-13f1-56a8-b31d-e09c5ab7b4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281990} {:answer/id #uuid "0866ed22-845e-5ab1-a35e-f91ca2a59c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281991} {:answer/id #uuid "08355e7d-0feb-5ac0-b0c7-65e11ff8854f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0866ed22-845e-5ab1-a35e-f91ca2a59c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281991} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc2ca994-0989-5916-a443-23802213f316" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9532e0ca-ce7a-5b85-b57a-a7477a29240f" :question/math-academy-id "q-87821" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $3(2-5x)^{9}+5\\le 8.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the ninth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2-5x)^{9}+5 & \\le 8 \\\\ 3(2-5x)^{9} & \\le 3 \\\\ (2-5x)^{9} & \\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the ninth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[9]{(2-5x)^{9}} & \\le \\sqrt[9]{1} \\\\ 2-5x & \\le 1 \\\\ -5x & \\le -1 \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2463ef2-c276-53cb-a1a1-8601789574d3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power Compared To a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6886689b-3005-561f-af07-8517e735ede5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281995} {:answer/id #uuid "131b6490-fe1a-5e75-ae49-6db2a8f3e772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281996} {:answer/id #uuid "d6fd93db-1455-5d37-b5dd-4f3e5ab0ac7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281997} {:answer/id #uuid "87d16f6b-4848-59b0-9033-d16ae112d4c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-1$ or $x>3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281998} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec98b40-e13f-5fd1-9cc4-e4a7f5e630ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6fd93db-1455-5d37-b5dd-4f3e5ab0ac7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281997} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9c6461-769c-5e9f-bf27-ec0c90bd348e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee05bf6b-6998-5677-acf5-d2a1f4ac5e65" :question/math-academy-id "q-87834" :question/problem "Solve $(x-3)^{6}+54>-10.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{6}+54 & >-10 \\\\ (x-3)^{6} & >-64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $(x-3)^{6}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(6)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2463ef2-c276-53cb-a1a1-8601789574d3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power Compared To a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ccddb8-23d8-5a5e-b176-d56875bdb723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282002} {:answer/id #uuid "b551695e-1671-5fd8-94ea-f80baf6e1505" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\sqrt[8]{3}<x<4+\\sqrt[8]{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282003} {:answer/id #uuid "dc6bd2a0-9484-5fbb-a365-34e91679b5d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282004} {:answer/id #uuid "da72e542-c152-5569-88fd-8da5a1191bdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>4-\\sqrt[8]{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282005} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ec9d79-9410-52c9-b379-581c3addb4b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\sqrt[8]{3}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ccddb8-23d8-5a5e-b176-d56875bdb723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282002} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8c04a2a-fd78-5c00-a0ae-bae8c11e5af1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac3e85e7-af86-52b0-aa01-fae3d5911c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-87835" :question/problem "Solve $(4-3x)^{8}+12<9.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the eighth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4-3x)^{8}+12 & <9 \\\\ (4-3x)^{8} & <-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(4-3x)^{8}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(8)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2463ef2-c276-53cb-a1a1-8601789574d3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power Compared To a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f818daf0-bb72-5dba-969c-400dbe0848a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282009} {:answer/id #uuid "0985fabf-fc3c-5366-a9b8-c2f8d9beb1ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\sqrt[8]{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282010} {:answer/id #uuid "eb75b420-c054-5dcf-bc94-5df4560f3469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282011} {:answer/id #uuid "49956feb-4a6e-56f8-86e5-bbd8b70b002d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt[8]{3}+2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282012} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec19bec-f934-5400-a79e-971068be8936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\sqrt[8]{5}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb75b420-c054-5dcf-bc94-5df4560f3469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282011} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4c59a84-8d13-5b08-b645-e3d3b17cc346" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4b11c9e-fd4a-567c-aa0f-0eef7726e56c" :question/math-academy-id "q-87840" :question/problem "Solve $4(2-x)^{8}+3\\ge -9.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the eighth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2-x)^{8}+3 & \\ge -9 \\\\ 4(2-x)^{8} & \\ge -12 \\\\ (2-x)^{8} & \\ge -3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $(2-x)^{8}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(8)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2107f945-7cfa-5abd-a6c1-bf15d5039e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c65d21b-8d27-540f-9396-0f665d23cd5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le 5+\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282016} {:answer/id #uuid "210d0b1f-1b29-55df-9b13-e552c960a58a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -5-\\sqrt{2}\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge 5-\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282017} {:answer/id #uuid "8934b52b-f1bc-5f98-bf08-742e9aacdd80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\sqrt{2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282018} {:answer/id #uuid "c07c0cfd-bbf4-5542-a9db-9268e868d011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 5-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282019} {:answer/id #uuid "0a65cf1e-cfc8-5554-87de-e4021b9fb18c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c65d21b-8d27-540f-9396-0f665d23cd5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le 5+\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282016} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cdb7af8-7881-58d7-816c-44a68432625b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fceb2ee0-c860-5eb1-97cf-5d41fec4b50b" :question/math-academy-id "q-87918" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(5-x)^{2}+4\\le 6.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the quadratic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-x)^{2}+4 & \\le 6 \\\\ (5-x)^{2} & \\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the square root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(5-x)^{2}} & \\le \\sqrt{2} \\\\ |5-x| & \\le \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{2}\\le 5-x\\le \\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2}\\le 5-x & \\le \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}-5\\le -x & \\le \\sqrt{2}-5 \\\\ 5+\\sqrt{2}\\ge x & \\ge 5-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the lower number is on the left:\n\n$$\n5-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le 5+\\sqrt{2}\n$$"}]}
